- U>R | plan to turn the top floor into a place full of life again | v: stimulation, benevolence | chance: 72
- B>G | rent the spare rooms to pay for the roof, so it stays in the family | v: security, tradition | chance: 74
- R>W | ring every sibling tonight and promise they will always have a room | binds | v: benevolence, conformity | chance: 80
- G>U | learn the house from them first: the boiler, the garden, the old stories | v: tradition, self-direction | mark: learned a skill | chance: 80
works: The house is settled without a quarrel, and {parent} rests easy.
works: The old rooms fill with life again.
fails not W G: The siblings hear of it and feel passed over.
